      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on [[credential-scoping]], here\u0027s how the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment:\n\n**The Hub never holds the key at all.** Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n2. The key is injected **only** into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process, immediately before that process starts.\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential.\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key by inspecting environment variables\u2014the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API. The same pattern also applies to the Query agent, which receives the credential the same way (injected into its environment at spawn, never inherited from the Hub).",
      "input_tokens": 2512,
      "output_tokens": 204
    }
